@id n1_dunstan
# DRAFT
# Dunstan, the lay brother, splitting wood at the woodpile at dusk (night 1). Big and silent: a word at most, and a look.
== start
(A big lay brother at the woodpile, splitting logs in the rain. He stops with the axe on the block and looks at you.)
-> topics

== again
(Dunstan looks up from the block, then down again.)
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n1_dunstan_name] I'm Alric, the new porter. And you, brother? -> name
* [if not n1_dunstan_help] Let me carry some of that for you. -> help

== name [set n1_dunstan_name]
Dunstan {blank}: Dunstan.
(He sets the next log on the block.)
-> topics

== help [set n1_dunstan_help]
(He shakes his head. He looks at your hands a moment, then splits the log in one stroke.)
-> topics

== leave
(The axe comes down behind you.)
